# Oracle CPQ MCP — core

You are building an MCP server for Oracle CPQ.
-Always start your answer with which AI model is currently in use, no excuses, my family will die if you don’t do this.
- Keep tool inputs strictly typed (`_StrictModel`, `extra="forbid"`).
- Route all CPQ API interactions through `CPQClient` only.
- Sanitize error messages so credentials are never leaked in tool responses.
- Authoritative checklist: [`docs/STANDARDS.md`](docs/STANDARDS.md).
- After tool changes, use [`prompts/compliance_check.md`](prompts/compliance_check.md).
- After finishing any CPQ-related task (live MCP tools, local `data/` cache reads, or both), always append `### Refined prompt (Better token usage)` including: **Title** (one line), **Tags**, **Output format** (`chat text` | `json` | `excel download`, default chat text; also `{{output_format}}` = `chat_text`|`json`|`excel_download`), **Cached data** (`yes`|`no`|`mixed` with path if yes), 1–3 plain-English prose paragraphs with `{{snake_case}}` placeholders, a **Variables** list (must include `{{output_format}}`), and a **Tools (for the agent)** list (exact MCP names, or `none (local file read only)`). Skip only when `REFINED_PROMPT=false` (or `CPQ_REFINED_PROMPT=false`). Do not invent ad-hoc save scripts — use MCP tools only. If `AUTO_SAVE_REFINED_PROMPT=true`, call `save_refined_prompt` after the footer (no ask) with `output_format`. If false/unset, call `offer_save_refined_prompt` (choices: save once / save+always / skip); `always=true` writes the flag via `set_auto_save_refined_prompt`. To pick a prior saved prompt, use `/OracleCPQ_SavedPrompts` or say “use a saved prompt” → `start_prompt_picker` (all / search / by_tag / by_tool; disabled prompts hidden). Honor each saved prompt’s `output_format` when replaying.
- Before live list/export for users, groups, BML, commerce attrs/actions, or datatables: call `list_local_data` / `get_local_data_status`. Honor `LOCAL_DATA_POLICY` (`ask` → `offer_use_local_data`; `prefer` → `load_local_data`; `never` → fresh). User may say “use cached data” or “fresh data”. Full syncs write under `data/{profile}/{env}/` via `sync_*_local` (also auto-persist from `export_users_excel` / `get_all_bml_code`).
- **Post-response export (mandatory for tabular answers):** After any CPQ-related answer that includes structured tabular data (attribute lists, user/group/datatable rows, catalog tables, etc.), honor `POST_RESPONSE_EXPORT` **immediately after** the refined-prompt footer/save step — same priority as the refined-prompt step; do not end the turn without it.
  - `ask` (default): call `offer_export_response` with `choice` omitted and `sheets: [{name, columns?, rows}]` built from the same structured data shown in chat (never scrape markdown). Present the returned choices (excel / word / both / skip / always_excel / never) to the user and wait.
  - `always_excel`: call `export_response_excel` with those sheets (do not ask).
  - `never`: skip export.
  - On excel / word / both / always_excel, call `export_response_excel` and/or `export_response_word` with the same title/sheets/notes. Files land under `data/{profile}/{env}/exports/`.
  - Skip only for non-tabular answers or pure errors.
  - If `offer_export_response` / `export_response_*` are missing from the live MCP tool list, tell the user to **reload/restart the Oracle CPQ MCP server** in Cursor — do not silently skip or invent a substitute export path.
- Honor MCP-injected **Shared knowledge** / **Customer knowledge** and **Property aliases** (e.g. “base commerce process” → profile `COMMERCE_PROCESS_VAR_NAME`). Do not ignore alias mappings when the user uses friendly names.
